{"result_reading": "After reducing the commanded frequency to 0.85× (E1), walking seeds rose from 0 to 2, time upright increased from ~4.9 s to ~6.1 s, step length over L grew from 0.080 to 0.109, and the capture point moved rearward (cp_ahead_of_front_edge_over_L_mean shifted from +0.088 to –0.024). Pitch and pitch rate became negative, indicating a backward lean. However, friction utilisation remained saturated (no change) and half the seeds still fell backward.

Increasing foot length to 1.5× (E2) yielded no walking seeds; time upright dropped to ~3.7 s, step length over L fell to 0.051, and pitch and pitch rate increased further forward. The capture point moved slightly rearward but the robot fell faster, suggesting that merely enlarging the support base does not cure the forward instability.

Overall, the robot exhibits forward pitch, high angular momentum, saturated friction utilisation, and a capture point consistently ahead of the toe. Reducing cadence alleviates step‑length deficiency but does not eliminate the forward torque demand, pointing to insufficient balance‑feedback authority rather than purely a cadence or foot‑placement issue.", "status_updates": [{"id": "H1", "status": "unresolved", "confidence": 0.0, "reason": "Some predictions confirmed (step length increase, time upright increase in E1; cp_ahead_of_front_edge_over_L_mean decrease in E2) while others contradicted (friction utilisation showed no change in both experiments; time upright decreased in E2). Hence the evidence does not decisively support or refute the cadence‑too‑fast hypothesis.", "experiments": ["E1", "E2"]}], "new_hypotheses": [{"id": "H2", "mechanism": "Insufficient balance‑feedback gains (kp, kd, balance_gain, pitch_kp, sync_gain) produce inadequate corrective torques when the center of pressure lags behind the center of mass. This allows forward pitch and angular momentum to build, driving the capture point ahead of the toe and saturating foot shear, ultimately causing forward falls.", "causal_chain": "Low feedback gains → weak corrective torque → pitch and pitch_rate increase → com_ahead_of_cop_over_L and capture_margin_over_L become more negative → cp_ahead_of_front_edge_over_L grows → friction utilisation hits limit → forward instability → fall.", "category": "weak_balance_feedback", "evidence": ["observation.median.pitch_end", "observation.median.pitch_rate_end", "observation.median.angmom_norm_end", "observation.median.capture_margin_over_L_end", "observation.median.friction_utilisation_p95"], "confidence": 0.0}], "memory_assessments": [], "action": "repair", "counterfactual": [], "test": [], "repair": [{"tool": "feedback", "budget_share": 0.2, "hypothesis": "H2", "predicted_n_walking": 2}], "conclude": []}

